<Layout title="Sources & credits"><PageIntro eyebrow="A story with a record" title="Where the information comes from." description="This redesign draws on the foundation’s archived website, public profiles, partner materials, and nonprofit filings. Historical information is kept in context." /><section class="section container article-grid"><div class="prose"><h2>The foundation’s archive.</h2><ol class="sources-list">{sources.map(([name, date, url]) => <li><a href={url}>{name} ↗</a><small>Wayback Machine capture: {date}</small></li>)}</ol><h2>Public records and partner sources.</h2><ul><li><a href="https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/364631367">ProPublica Nonprofit Explorer</a> — IRS-derived financial records and nonprofit identity.</li><li><a href="https://agroforestryrc.org/">Agroforestry Regeneration Communities</a> — partner context and project photography.</li><li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/abundant-earth-foundation">AEF on LinkedIn</a> and <a href="https://linktr.ee/abundantearthfoundation">Linktree</a> — public descriptions and linked profiles.</li></ul><h2>Photography and design.</h2><p>Project photographs are drawn from AEF’s archived materials and ARC’s public website. They remain the property of their respective rights holders. Captions identify the source and distinguish contextual photography from verified depictions of a specific project.</p><p>Imagery includes Contour Lines in Guatemala, Permaculture Paradise Institute in Malawi, Refarmers in Uganda, and archived material from Towards Green Environment, Beyond Organic Design, and the Youth in Permaculture Prize.</p><p>The botanical mark and website treatment are redesign concepts. The fonts are Fraunces and DM Sans, distributed under the SIL Open Font License and served locally.</p><h2>What has not been assumed.</h2><p>Historical project status, award plans, team roles, and statistics have not been silently promoted to current facts. No invented testimonials, grant totals, payment confirmations, or subscriber counts are used.</p><p class="source-note">Research reviewed September 18, 2026. Archived source availability can change. Asset provenance and original URLs are also documented in the repository.</p></div><aside class="aside-card"><h3>Help improve the record.</h3><p>If you lead a project, hold image rights, or have more recent information, we welcome an update.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/?topic=Project%20update">Share an update</a></aside></section></Layout>
